      },
      "description": "EXPERIMENTAL. The repeated-route idea comes from Packfade's approach (https://github.com/pgodlews/packfade, MIT licence) by the same author; the fit reuses its Huber-WLS and day-clustered bootstrap.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Experimental.** Routes the car drives often (found from trip start/end points, distance and the road taken) are used as a repeatable test: on the same route at matched conditions, energy per distance should be stable, so a lasting drift points at tyres and pressures, alignment, a dragging brake or added load.\n\nEnergy is the BMS count (state of charge used), not the 30 s pack-power samples. Rain, wind and load are not measured.\n\nIdea from [Packfade](https://github.com/pgodlews/packfade) (MIT) by the same author."
      }
